@startuml
title Figure 4.12: Sequence Diagram of the Analyze Code Coverage.
actor User
participant "Vue\n(Coverage.vue)" as Vue
participant "Rust\n(coverage.rs)" as Rust
participant "coverage.py" as Cov
database "SQLite" as DB
entity "coverage.json" as JSON

note over Vue: manual tab OR autoRun=1 from Execute post-run modal
Vue -> Rust: check_coverage_installed(interpreter)
alt not installed
    Vue -> Rust: install_dependencies(["coverage"])
end

User -> Vue: select source / test files
Vue -> Rust: run_coverage(projectId, path, ...)
Rust -> Cov: coverage erase
Rust -> Cov: coverage run --branch -m pytest
Rust -> Cov: coverage json -o coverage.json
Cov --> Rust: status
Rust -> JSON: write coverage.json + meta.json
Rust -> Rust: parse JSON (format 1/2)
Rust --> Vue: event coverage-finished {summary}
Rust -> DB: save coverage_result + coverage_history

User -> Vue: click a source file
Vue -> Rust: get_coverage_detail(filePath)
Rust -> JSON: read coverage.json + source
Rust --> Vue: four-state line data
Vue -> Vue: render highlighted viewer + function filter

alt export report
    User -> Vue: Export (JSON / CSV)
    Vue -> Rust: export_coverage_report(projectId, format)
end
@enduml
